iven-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gatter</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phosphorylated KDR is expressed in the neoplastic and stromal elements of human renal tumours and shuttles from cell membrane to nucleus</article-title><source>J Pathol</source><year>2004</year><volume>202</volume><fpage>313</fpage><lpage>320</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Pathol||202|313||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14991896</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gelb</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Renal cell carcinoma: current prognostic factors. Union Internationale Contre le Cancer (UICC) and the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC)</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1997</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>981</fpage><lpage>986</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||80|981||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9307202</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gelb</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Sudilovsky</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Medeiros</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Appraisal of intratumoral microvessel density, MIB-1 score, DNA content, and p53 protein expression as prognostic indicators in patients with locally confined renal cell carcinoma</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1997</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>1768</fpage><lpage>1775</lpage><!--Pub